# MadGraph5 batch script: p p > j j inside a jet-HT window.
#
# The pp_to_jj row's card (shipped defaults, ebeam 6500, NNPDF23_lo_as_0130_qed
# through LHAPDF) with htjmin = 300 and htjmax = 800: the HT-binned QCD shape the
# CMS survey's HT samples use, on the cheapest process that reaches it. The
# jet sum htj runs over gluons and the four light-flavour quarks (maxjetflavor
# 4); with two jets it is 2 pT, so the window is pT in [150, 400] and is
# aligned with the ptj cut a reference can already read. That alignment is the
# cell's blind spot: it cannot tell a scalar from a vector sum or see which
# jets enter a sum of more than two.
generate p p > j j
output pp_to_jj_ht -nojpeg
launch
  set ebeam1 6500
  set ebeam2 6500
  set pdlabel lhapdf
  set lhaid 247000
  set htjmin 300
  set htjmax 800
  done
